note top of Staff
**Inheritance**
The one-task-per-turn rule is written once in
Staff's final ({leaf}) methods: startTurn, waitTurn,
markActed. Subclasses add only their own actions.
end note
note right of Customer
**Abstraction / Template Method**
abstract typeLabel() and satisfactionLossPerTurn().
The final ({leaf}) applyWaitingPenalty() calls the
subclass's satisfactionLossPerTurn().
end note
note bottom of Order
**Encapsulation**
lockPrice() throws if the price is already locked.
State changes (advanceUnit, markServed, markPaid)
are package-private (~).
end note
note bottom of VIPCustomer
**Polymorphism**
VIPCustomer overrides applyCustomerPricing() (pays 90%).
CriticCustomer overrides onServed() (+10 if served within
2 turns of ordering, otherwise -10). Control and Boundary
classes never test a customer's type.
end note
note bottom of HappyHourPolicy
**Single responsibility**
All Happy Hour rules in one class: availability,
2-turn duration, 20% off, +15 recovery.
BillCalculator uses it.
end note
note bottom of ComboMeal
**Inheritance + aggregation**
A ComboMeal is a MenuItem and holds two base
MenuItems. Overrides describe(); price is 90%
of the two dishes.
end note
note bottom of Money
**Used by** (dependencies not drawn,
to keep the diagram readable):
ConsoleUI, GameController, HappyHourPolicy
Cashier, ComboMeal, MenuItem
VIPCustomer
end note
note bottom of ActionResult
**Used by** (dependencies not drawn,
